<article class="env-remark" id="562B2A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/562B2A">Remark <span data-tag="562B2A">4.2.2.5</span>.</a> In most applications of Proposition <a href="/tag/BFE09D" data-tag="BFE09D">4.2.2.4</a>, we will have $Y = S$. In that case, $Y^{p'_{S}/}$ can be identified with $S$, and the conclusion is that the projection $X^{p_ S/} \rightarrow S$ is a Cartesian fibration. </p>
